From 750598dacf702556c0ec681e0964096e62b35025 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Geonmo Ryu <geonmo@kisti.re.kr>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] nfs, xrootd: report the capacity of the pools or a space
 reservation

Motivation:
Clients can't see how much space dCache has. The NFS door reports a
fixed size of 1 EiB, so df on an NFS mount is of no use to users or
monitoring. The xrootd door doesn't answer kXR_Qspace at all, so
`xrdfs spaceinfo` fails and df hides xrootdfs mounts (size 0).

Modification:
Add dcache.capacity.source, inherited by nfs.capacity.source and
xrootd.capacity.source:

- namespace (default): a fixed 1 EiB, as the NFS door reports today
- pools: the total and free space of all online pools, counting
  removable replicas as free, as the frontend does for SRR
- reservation: the size and available space of a space reservation,
  given by dcache.capacity.reservation or, for xrootd, by the
  WriteToken tag of the queried path, as the FTP door does for
  SITE USAGE

Capacity.Provider computes the value for both doors and logs a failure
once, until the capacity can be determined again. The NFS door keeps
the namespace file counts and falls back to the namespace statistics on
failure. As NFS doesn't tell the door which export a request is for,
'reservation' needs a space token there, or the door fails to start.
The xrootd door answers kXR_Qspace in the format of xrootd's oss plugin
for paths the user can access.

Result:
By default, NFS is unchanged, and xrootd clients now see 1 EiB, so df
shows xrootdfs mounts. Disk-only sites can report the capacity of their
pools, and sites using space reservations the capacity of a reservation.

Fixes: #8275
Target: master
